# Derived from ledger.jsonl and rebuilt whenever they fall behind it. The ledger
# is the record and is kept; these are a reading of it, and a reading committed
# to git is one that can be wrong in a way nobody notices.
boards.json
index.json

# 2026-09-12: this rule is also stated by name in the root .gitignore, and
# that is the one to rely on. This file is tracked, so a rename carries it
# along and leaves the old path's derived readings covered by nothing -- which
# is what happened at 43bbfb2. The reasoning above is still the reasoning;
# only its reach was wrong.
